+
+// X81 (b1816, Rule Checker X81: capture timeout decisions). Runtime data flag X81_TAB[1], read first; 0 = off.
+// Bit 1 (T30+CFX): the 16-round capture timeout spares a due reward when the running timer started within 30 rounds of the
+// capture's start (a contest restarts the timer but not cap_start), with the due round from group_capture_pay_rounds (an allied
+// Capture holder counts, GameRules 196). Bit 2 (ARR): the first step onto the region (cap_on < 0) after a walk of 17+ rounds is
+// not dropped: cap_start moves up to 16 rounds before the arrival, so the due-reward test sees the timer that starts now.
+#define X81_BITS 0
+inline const volatile int X81_TAB[2] = { 0x58383131, X81_BITS }; // slot 0 magic keeps it out of .bss
+#define X81_ON(b) ((X81_TAB[1] & (b)) != 0)
